{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>May he enter, etc.</b> [May the righteous] enter in peace to their graves, like the sense of 'in peace you shall die' (Jeremiah 34:5) and 'you shall come to your fathers in peace' (Genesis 15:15):" "<b>They shall rest on their beds.</b> Everyone who walks straight before HaShem, like the sense of 'after YHWH your Elohim you shall walk' (Deuteronomy 13:5). And others say: 'peace' comes joined with 'the quiet one,' and they shall rest on their beds:" "<b>Walking straight before Him.</b> [And behold, נכוחו] is in place of נכחו, for the noun patterns change:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 57, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:54.514118577Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}